        "# Missing Value Analysis and Handling - Nikhil G\n",
        "This section follows the missing-value approach in the Complete Reference Notebook.\n",
        "- First, inspect missing values using counts and percentages.\n",
        "- Treat zero values in budget and revenue as unavailable values for this project baseline. This is an assumption and should be confirmed by the team.\n",
        "- Exclude highly sparse collection fields and free-text/image-path columns from the baseline dataset instead of filling them with artificial values.\n",
        "- For the selected modelling predictors, fill numerical missing values with the median and categorical missing values with the most frequent value."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "S56-1PSb8Clu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df_clean = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "missing_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'Missing Count': df_clean.isnull().sum(),\n",
        "    'Missing Percentage': (df_clean.isnull().mean() * 100).round(2)\n",
        "}).sort_values(by='Missing Percentage', ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "display(missing_summary[missing_summary['Missing Count'] > 0])\n",
        "\n",
        "missing_plot = missing_summary[missing_summary['Missing Count'] > 0]\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
        "sns.barplot(\n",
